---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SECTIONS } from "../data/sections";

const title = "Cyber Monday Walking Pad Deals (2026): 6 Pads, Prices Checked";
const description =
  "Cyber Monday is 30 Nov 2026. On 27 Nov the WalkingPad Z1 was $265, the C2 $363 and the UREVO CyberPad $349 on Amazon: 3 of 6 pads at or below our target.";

const PRODUCTS = [
  {
    id: "walkingpad-z1",
    name: "WalkingPad Z1",
    brand: "WalkingPad",
    category: "Best Folding Pad This Cyber Monday",
    badge: "Best Folding Pad",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H2YYZTL8?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31oMu9TYTUL._SL500_.jpg","width":448,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: "/walkingpad-z1-review/",
    priceRange: "About $265 (Amazon, 27 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":265,"high":265},
    specs: "47.6 in. belt length · 1–4 mph · 242 lb capacity (WalkingPad) · about 50 lb · 4.1 in. high · folds in half",
    pros: [
      "At $265.04 on Amazon on 27 November it was below the $269 we set as a real deal in October",
      "A 47.6-inch belt, long enough for a normal stride, on a pad that folds in half for storage",
      "The listing describes a brushless motor and a 4.1-inch profile",
      "WalkingPad’s own store had the white version at $279, so the Amazon price is not an outlier",
    ],
    cons: [
      "No incline and no handlebar",
      "A 242 lb limit leaves little margin for heavier walkers",
      "Motor ratings conflict between sources, so the card leaves horsepower off",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The pad to buy on Cyber Monday if it is still $269 or less and you want a long belt that folds away.",
    description: "The Z1 has been the most consistent price on our walking pad watch list: $299 on WalkingPad’s own store on 28 October, with a $329 “compare at” price, and $299 on Amazon on 20 October. On 27 November Amazon listed it at $265.04, the first price we have recorded below our $269 target, and WalkingPad’s store had the white Z1 at $279 and the grey at $299. The Amazon listing gives a 47.6-inch walking belt, a 1 to 4 mph speed range, a 4.1-inch height and a weight of about 50 lb, and describes a brushless motor and a fold-in-half design that halves its footprint for storage. WalkingPad’s specifications, recorded in our Z1 review, give a 242 lb maximum user weight. It is a walking pad, not a jogging pad: 4 mph is a brisk walk. If the Cyber Monday price is at or below Black Friday’s, this is the safest buy on the page; if it has gone back to $299, wait for the next sale.",
  },
  {
    id: "walkingpad-c2",
    name: "WalkingPad C2",
    brand: "WalkingPad",
    category: "Most Compact Pad",
    badge: "Most Compact",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F48MZV54?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31WUvcjXp-L._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $363 (Amazon, 27 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":363,"high":363},
    specs: "1–4 mph · 220 lb capacity · 55 lb · folds 180° to 5.4 in. high · remote, app and FootSense control (listing)",
    pros: [
      "At $362.57 on Amazon and $379 on WalkingPad’s store it met our $379 target on both",
      "Folds in half to 5.4 inches high, light enough at 55 lb to move on its wheels",
      "Arrives assembled; speed by remote, app or the listing’s FootSense control",
      "About $66 below the $429 it sold for through most of October",
    ],
    cons: [
      "A 220 lb limit, the lowest here",
      "A narrow belt that some walkers find constricting",
      "WalkingPad’s return shipping is estimated from $100 for this model",
    ],
    bottomLine: "A real Black Friday price for the most compact pad here. Buy on Cyber Monday at $379 or less if you are well under 220 lb.",
    description: "The C2 is WalkingPad’s compact folding pad, and for most of October it sat at $429 against a $599 “compare at” price on WalkingPad’s own store, which is why our Black Friday page said $379 or less would be a deal. On 27 November WalkingPad listed it at exactly $379 and Amazon at $362.57, so the target is met on both. The Amazon listing gives a 1 to 4 mph speed range, a 220 lb maximum user weight, a 55 lb machine weight, a 2.0 HP motor and a 180-degree folding design that is 5.4 inches high when folded; it arrives assembled and runs from the remote or app. WalkingPad also sells a C2 Mini at $399 and C2 desk bundles from $528, which are different products, so check what is in your basket. Because WalkingPad deducts return shipping estimated from $100 for this model if you buy direct and change your mind, the Amazon price with Amazon’s return terms may be the better buy for a first pad.",
  },
  {
    id: "urevo-cyberpad",
    name: "UREVO CyberPad for Office",
    brand: "UREVO",
    category: "Best Incline Pad Price",
    badge: "Best With Incline",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F6LJGZ12?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/410+XTzfCUL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $349 (Amazon, 27 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":349,"high":349},
    specs: "0–14% auto incline · 0.6–4.0 mph · 2.5 HP brushless motor (listing) · slim under-desk profile",
    pros: [
      "At $349.25 on Amazon it was $82.74 below the $431.99 we recorded on 6 November",
      "Below our $389 target and below UREVO’s own store price of $369.99 to $399.99",
      "A 14% powered incline, the steepest on this page, adjustable while you walk",
      "The listing describes a brushless motor and a slim profile for under-desk storage",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Capacity figures conflict between UREVO’s page, the Amazon listing and the manual",
      "UREVO’s return window is 14 days, unused, if you buy direct",
      "Top speed of 4 mph, like most pads",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The clearest real price cut on this page. Buy on Cyber Monday at about $350 if you want incline under a desk.",
    description: "The CyberPad for Office is UREVO’s steep-incline desk pad, and it is the pad on this page with the clearest genuine drop. Amazon listed it at $431.99 on 6 November, when our Black Friday walking pad page set $389 as the price at which it would be a deal; on 27 November the same listing was $349.25, and UREVO’s own store had it at $369.99 to $399.99 against a $479.99 “compare at” price. UREVO lists a 0 to 14% auto incline and a 0.6 to 4.0 mph range, and the Amazon listing describes a 2.5 HP brushless motor and quiet operation. The figure to check is the weight limit: UREVO’s page, the Amazon listing and the manual have given different capacities, so read the one on the listing you buy. Incline is what keeps a pad useful once a 4 mph walk feels easy, which is why this is the pad we would buy if you want more effort without running. UREVO advertises a 30-day price match on its store if you would rather buy direct.",
  },
  {
    id: "merach-w50",
    name: "MERACH W50 Walking Pad",
    brand: "MERACH",
    category: "Best for Heavier Walkers",
    badge: "Highest Capacity",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F6NHNQK9?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41LxzDBxUsL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $256 (Amazon, 27 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":256,"high":256},
    specs: "400 lb capacity · 12% auto incline · up to 4.0 mph · 16.5 x 41.3 in. belt · 3.5 HP brushless (peak, listing)",
    pros: [
      "A 400 lb rating, the highest on this page, consistent between MERACH and the listing",
      "A 12% powered incline",
      "About $43 below the $299.99 MERACH listed on 18 October",
      "LED display and app, per the listing",
    ],
    cons: [
      "$7.49 above the $249 we set as a real deal",
      "A 41.3-inch belt is short for taller walkers",
      "The motor figure is a peak rating; MERACH gives 1.25 HP continuous",
    ],
    bottomLine: "Watch it on Cyber Monday. At $249 or less it is the best-value incline pad for heavier walkers.",
    description: "The W50 is the pick for heavier walkers because its weight rating is consistent across sources. The Amazon listing gives a 400 lb capacity, a 12% auto incline, a 4.0 mph top speed, a 16.5 by 41.3-inch belt and a 3.5 HP brushless motor, and MERACH’s own page, recorded on our Black Friday walking pad page, gave a 1.25 HP continuous rating with the same 3.5 HP peak, which is a more honest figure than most pads publish. Its price history is also the most informative of any pad here: $299.99 on MERACH’s store on 18 October against $479.99, about $297 on Amazon in September, and a brief promo-code drop to about $198 in July. On 27 November this listing was $256.49, $7.49 above the $249 target. It is the pad to watch on Monday. Check you have the W50 and not the W50 Lite, a cheaper sibling with lower ratings.",
  },
  {
    id: "urevo-strol-2e-pro",
    name: "UREVO Strol 2E Pro",
    brand: "UREVO",
    category: "Cheapest Pad With Incline and a Handle",
    badge: "Under $200",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H1H4JT4C?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/410e3-vj4nL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $178 (Amazon, 27 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":178,"high":178},
    specs: "12% manual incline · 0.6–4 mph walking, 0.4–6.2 mph running mode · 300 lb (UREVO) · 44 lb · folding handle",
    pros: [
      "A 12% manual incline and a handle for under $180",
      "UREVO lists a 300 lb maximum load, more than the flat Strol 2E’s 265 lb",
      "Light at 44 lb and folds without tools, per the listing",
      "Amazon listings ranged from $161.49 to $177.64, close to UREVO’s $171.99",
    ],
    cons: [
      "The incline is set by hand before you walk, not from the remote",
      "No earlier price record, so we cannot say how much of a saving it is",
      "Several listings for the same pad; check the bullets match",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The cheapest way into incline and a jogging mode. Pay $165 or less and choose the listing whose bullets match.",
    description: "The Strol 2E Pro replaces the flat Strol 2E on this page because it adds a 12% incline for about $10 more on UREVO’s store. UREVO lists it at $171.99 against a $259.99 “compare at” price, with up to 12% manual incline, a 2.25 HP motor, a 300 lb maximum load and a 44 lb frame, and the Amazon listing on this card describes a 0.6 to 4 mph walking mode and a 0.4 to 6.2 mph running mode with the handle raised. On 27 November Amazon had three Strol 2E Pro listings at $161.49, $168.29 and $177.64, so shop by the bullets rather than the first result; this card shows the $177.64 listing. The incline is manual, set before you start, so it suits walkers who will pick one incline for a session rather than change it mid-walk. We have no earlier price for it, so we would treat the lowest of those listings as the price to beat. UREVO’s app registration adds 180 days to its warranty.",
  },
  {
    id: "walkingpad-r3-hybrid-plus",
    name: "WalkingPad R3 Hybrid+",
    brand: "WalkingPad",
    category: "Best Premium Pad to Watch",
    badge: "Best Premium",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F8VSLK43?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31EHF8W4eGL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $722 (Amazon, 27 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":722,"high":722},
    specs: "47.2 x 17.3 in. walking area · 1–7.5 mph · 265 lb capacity · side handrails · aluminium frame · folds",
    pros: [
      "The longest, widest deck here and a top speed for an easy jog",
      "Dual side handrails that lower for desk walking, per the listing",
      "Arrives fully assembled",
      "About $77 below the $799 it sold for through October",
    ],
    cons: [
      "$22.65 above the $699 we set as a real deal",
      "No incline at this price",
      "WalkingPad deducts return shipping on direct returns (from $120 for the R1 Pro and R2)",
    ],
    bottomLine: "Watch it on Cyber Monday. At $699 or less it is the pad to buy if you want to jog as well as walk.",
    description: "The R3 Hybrid+ is the premium pad on this page, and its case is the deck: WalkingPad lists a 47.2 by 17.3-inch walking area, 1 to 7.5 mph and a 265 lb capacity, and the Amazon listing describes dual side handrails that lower for under-desk walking, an aluminium alloy frame, a status light strip and a double-folding design for upright storage. It arrives assembled. In October it sat at $799 against $999 on WalkingPad’s store for weeks, which is why we set $699 as the Black Friday target. On 27 November WalkingPad’s store had it at $759 and Amazon at $721.65, so it has moved but not far enough. Check the version in your basket: WalkingPad’s R3 range includes a plain R3 at $549 to $599 and an R3 Hybrid that was sold out. There is no incline, so you are paying for belt size and rails rather than features.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "By Price", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/price/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Cyber Monday Walking Pad Deals", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/cyber-monday-walking-pad-deals/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "When is Cyber Monday 2026?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Monday 30 November 2026, the Monday after Thanksgiving. Many stores run Cyber Week offers into early December, and some Black Friday prices carry over to the Monday.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is a good Cyber Monday price for a walking pad?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "One below what the same pad sold for in October, not below its “compare at” price. On our checks, $269 or less for a WalkingPad Z1, $379 or less for a C2 and about $389 or less for a UREVO CyberPad for Office were real deals; all three were there on 27 November.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is it better to buy a walking pad on Black Friday or Cyber Monday?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "There is no consistent answer. Some pads hold the same price all weekend, some sell out and a few drop again on Monday. If a pad has already reached your target price, buying on Friday avoids the risk of it selling out.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Will a walking pad ordered on Cyber Monday arrive by Christmas?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Usually, yes, because pads ship as parcels. WalkingPad’s FAQ gives 1 to 2 business days of processing and 3 to 5 of shipping, and UREVO’s 5 to 7 working days once tracking is issued. Check the delivery date on the listing.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is Amazon or the maker’s store cheaper for walking pads?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "On 27 November 2026 Amazon was a little cheaper for four of five pads we compared. The makers’ stores have their own terms: WalkingPad deducts return shipping from about $100, and UREVO allows 14 days for unused returns. Both advertised price matching.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-27",
      dateModified: "2026-11-27",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      ...(product.brand ? { brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.brand } } : {}),
      ...(product.image ? { image: product.image.url } : {}),
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              ...(product.amazonUrl ? { url: product.amazonUrl } : {}),
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 6,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/cyber-monday-walking-pad-deals/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/cyber-monday-walking-pad-deals/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "price");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const MORE = (GROUP?.pages ?? []).filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-27",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-27",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "cyber monday walking pad deals",
      "walking pad cyber monday",
      "cyber monday walking pad",
      "walkingpad cyber monday",
      "under desk treadmill cyber monday",
      "walking pad deals",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Best Folding Pad: WalkingPad Z1", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/price/">By Price</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Cyber Monday 2026</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Cyber Monday Walking Pad Deals 2026</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        Cyber Monday falls on 30 November this year, and walking pads are the treadmills it suits best: they ship as parcels and arrive in days. We checked six pads on Black Friday, 27 November, against the prices we recorded in October. Three were at or below the price we said would make them a real deal; three were not. Here is each one, the price to wait for, and what to check before you click buy.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 27, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS<br />
          <span class="ed-method">How we chose: makers’ published specifications and manuals, independent reviews and owner reports, cross-checked. Not tested hands-on.</span>
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We may earn a commission when you buy through the links below. It costs you nothing and never decides a ranking. <a href="/editorial-standards/">How we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#walkingpad-z1"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31oMu9TYTUL._SL500_.jpg" alt="WalkingPad Z1" width="448" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#walkingpad-c2"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31WUvcjXp-L._SL500_.jpg" alt="WalkingPad C2" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#urevo-cyberpad"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/410+XTzfCUL._SL500_.jpg" alt="UREVO CyberPad for Office" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>WalkingPad Z1 · WalkingPad C2 · UREVO CyberPad for Office</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          Walking pads are discounted for most of the year, so a Cyber Monday badge on one tells you very little. What tells
          you something is the price history. In October our <a href="/black-friday-walking-pad-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Black Friday walking pad deals</a> page recorded what six
          popular pads were selling for and set a price at which each would become a genuine deal. On 27 November 2026 we
          checked those pads again, on Amazon through its product API and on the makers’ own stores, and added one new
          pick. This page gives the result. Cyber Monday prices can move either way from these, so treat them as the bar a
          Monday price has to beat, and check the current price before you buy.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Folding Pad:</span> <a href="#walkingpad-z1">WalkingPad Z1</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Most Compact:</span> <a href="#walkingpad-c2">WalkingPad C2</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best With Incline:</span> <a href="#urevo-cyberpad">UREVO CyberPad for Office</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Highest Capacity:</span> <a href="#merach-w50">MERACH W50 Walking Pad</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[3].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Under $200:</span> <a href="#urevo-strol-2e-pro">UREVO Strol 2E Pro</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[4].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Premium:</span> <a href="#walkingpad-r3-hybrid-plus">WalkingPad R3 Hybrid+</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[5].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <nav class="ed-toc not-prose" aria-label="In this roundup">
          <h2>In this roundup</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#short-answer">The Short Answer</a></li>
            <li><a href="#price-check">Prices Checked on 27 November Against October</a></li>
            <li><a href="#picks">Six Walking Pads to Check on Cyber Monday</a></li>
            <li><a href="#store-vs-amazon">Maker’s Store or Amazon: Where to Buy</a></li>
            <li><a href="#under-200">Cheaper Pads We Also Checked</a></li>
            <li><a href="#after">If You Miss Cyber Monday</a></li>
            <li><a href="#timing">Buy Now or Wait for Monday?</a></li>
            <li><a href="#which-pad">Which Pad Fits Which Buyer</a></li>
            <li><a href="#before-you-buy">What to Check Before You Click Buy</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>On Black Friday the WalkingPad Z1 ($265.04), WalkingPad C2 ($362.57) and UREVO CyberPad for Office
            ($349.25) were already at or below the price we set in October as a real deal on Amazon; buy them on Cyber
            Monday only if the price is the same or lower.</strong> The MERACH W50 and WalkingPad R3 Hybrid+ were close but
            not there, and the <a href="/urevo-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>UREVO</a> Strol 2E Pro is the cheapest pad here with incline and a handle.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>WalkingPad Z1:</strong> $265.04 on Amazon against our $269 target; $279 to $299 on WalkingPad’s store.</li>
            <li><strong>WalkingPad C2:</strong> $362.57 on Amazon and $379 on WalkingPad’s store, against our $379 target.</li>
