        <div id="timing" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Buy Now or Wait for Monday?</h2>
<p>
            There is no reliable rule. Some pads hold the same price from Black Friday to Cyber Monday, some sell out, and a
            few get a further cut on the Monday. What the price history suggests for these six:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Already at target (Z1, C2, CyberPad for Office).</strong> If the price on Monday is the same or
            lower, buy. If it has risen, the Black Friday price shows the level to wait for in December.</li>
            <li><strong>Close to target (MERACH W50, R3 Hybrid+).</strong> These are the two worth watching on Monday:
            $7 and $23 above our targets on Friday.</li>
            <li><strong>No history (Strol 2E Pro).</strong> About $160 to $178 across UREVO and three Amazon listings;
            the cheapest of those is the price to look for.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Christmas delivery is rarely the issue with a pad. WalkingPad’s FAQ says most US orders are processed in 1 to 2
            business days and then take about 3 to 5 business days to ship, and UREVO’s FAQ gives 5 to 7 working days once a
            tracking number is issued. A pad ordered on 30 November should arrive well before Christmas from either; check
            the delivery date on the listing to be sure. Full-size treadmills are different, as our <a href="/cyber-monday-treadmill-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Cyber Monday treadmill deals</a> page explains.
          </p>
