        <div id="common-mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>What Goes Wrong With Cyber Monday Walking Pad Deals</h2>
          <p>Walking pads are easy to buy in a sale and easy to buy badly. These are the mistakes the price history shows most often.</p>
          <ol class="ed-mistakes not-prose">
            <li>
              <h3>Measuring the saving against the “compare at” price</h3>
              <p>The UREVO Strol 2E showed $128 off on Black Friday but was only $8 below its October price. Compare with the last price you saw, or with the history above.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Buying the sibling model</h3>
              <p>The Strol 2E and 2E Pro, W50 and W50 Lite, and Z1 and Z1R are different pads. Check the model name and bullets in your basket.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Ignoring the return cost</h3>
              <p>WalkingPad’s direct returns deduct shipping estimated from $100. On a $300 pad that can wipe out the saving, so be sure before you buy direct.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Choosing a pad too small for you because it is cheap</h3>
              <p>The C2’s 220 lb limit and the W50’s 41-inch belt suit some walkers and not others. Check weight limit and belt length before price.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
