        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>When is Cyber Monday 2026?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Monday 30 November 2026, the Monday after Thanksgiving. Many stores run Cyber Week offers into early December, and some Black Friday prices carry over to the Monday.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is a good Cyber Monday price for a walking pad?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              One below what the same pad sold for in October, not below its “compare at” price. On our checks, $269 or less for a WalkingPad Z1, $379 or less for a C2 and about $389 or less for a UREVO CyberPad for Office were real deals; all three were there on 27 November.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is it better to buy a walking pad on Black Friday or Cyber Monday?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              There is no consistent answer. Some pads hold the same price all weekend, some sell out and a few drop again on Monday. If a pad has already reached your target price, buying on Friday avoids the risk of it selling out.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Will a walking pad ordered on Cyber Monday arrive by Christmas?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Usually, yes, because pads ship as parcels. WalkingPad’s FAQ gives 1 to 2 business days of processing and 3 to 5 of shipping, and UREVO’s 5 to 7 working days once tracking is issued. Check the delivery date on the listing.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is Amazon or the maker’s store cheaper for walking pads?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On 27 November 2026 Amazon was a little cheaper for four of five pads we compared. The makers’ stores have their own terms: WalkingPad deducts return shipping from about $100, and UREVO allows 14 days for unused returns. Both advertised price matching.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

